---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LegalArticle from "../components/LegalArticle.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy - Diald Club"
  description="Privacy policy for the Diald Club coffee tracking app."
  bodyClass="legal-page"
>
  <LegalArticle title="Privacy Policy" updated="4 July 2026">
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how Diald Club ("Diald", "the app", "we",
      "us") collects, uses, and protects your information when you use the Diald
      iOS app and website. By using Diald, you agree to the practices described
      below.
    </p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Account information.</strong> When you create an account we store
        your email address and, optionally, profile details such as your display name.
        Authentication is handled by Supabase and may use email, Apple, or Google
        sign-in.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your coffee content.</strong> The beans, brew sessions, brew steps,
        ratios, temperatures, timings, ratings, tasting notes, reminders, and related
        settings you add are stored so they can sync across your devices.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Device tokens.</strong> If you enable push notifications we store
        an Apple Push Notification service token so we can send brew reminders and
        related app notifications.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Subscription information.</strong> If you subscribe to Supporter Monthly,
        Apple handles payment. We store subscription entitlement status and transaction
        identifiers needed to unlock paid features and keep access in sync.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>AI provider settings.</strong> If you use AI analysis, your OpenAI
        or Anthropic API key is stored on your device in the iOS keychain. It is not
        stored on our servers.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use your information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        To provide the app's core features: logging brews, managing beans,
        saving recipes and steps, generating stats, syncing data, and reminding
        you to brew.
      </li>
      <li>
        To manage account access, password reset flows, sign-in providers,
        subscription entitlement, and account deletion requests.
      </li>
      <li>To send notifications you have opted into.</li>
      <li>To maintain, secure, debug, and improve the service.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>AI analysis</h2>
    <p>
      AI analysis is optional. When you run an analysis, the brew data selected
      by your filters is sent from your device to the AI provider you chose,
      currently OpenAI or Anthropic, using your own API key. Provider use is
      governed by that provider's terms and privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>How your information is shared</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell your personal information. Information is shared only in
      the following circumstances:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>With service providers.</strong> We use Supabase for authentication
        and app data storage, Apple services for purchases and notifications, and
        your selected AI provider only when you choose to run AI analysis.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>When required by law.</strong> We may disclose information if required
        to do so by law or valid legal process.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      We retain your information for as long as your account is active. You can
      delete beans, brews, reminders, and other content from within the app
      where those controls are available. When you delete your account, your
      associated account data is removed from our systems.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      We use reasonable safeguards to protect your information, including
      encrypted connections, Supabase row-level security, Apple Keychain storage
      for AI provider keys, and access controls. No method of transmission or
      storage is completely secure.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal
      information. To delete your account or make a request, use the in-app
      account deletion flow or contact us using the details below.
    </p>

    <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Diald is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly
      collect personal information from children under 13.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will
      revise the "Last updated" date at the top of this page. Continued use of
      the app after changes take effect constitutes acceptance of the updated
      policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, contact us at <a
        href="mailto:kyle@kylescudder.co.uk">kyle@kylescudder.co.uk</a
      >.
    </p>
  </LegalArticle>
</BaseLayout>
